{title: Set Their Hands To The Good Work}
{subtitle: Nehemiah 3:23; 6:15–16; 2:17–18}
{key: G}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [G] | [G] | [G] | [G] |
| [G] | [Em7] | [Em7] | [C] |
| [C] | [G] | [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Jerusalem lies in ruins now
The [Em7]gates have burned with fire
A [C]disgrace upon the land
But [G]hear the call to higher
Nehemiah speaks to the crowd
With a [Em7]gracious hand
The [C]king has spoken his word
[G]Now is the time to [D]stand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
So they [Em7]set their hands to the work
The [C]good work they began
From the [Am7]shadow of the past
To the [Dsus4]strength of the man
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Aza[G]riah son of Maaseiah
Be[Em7]side his house he stands
Next to [C]Benjamin and Hasshub
Re[G]building by God's com[D]mand
Son [G]of Ananiah he is
In the [Em7]list of the brave
Working [C]on the wall of the city
Where [G]the faithful have [D]grave
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Fif-ty-two days in the heat
The [Em]work is done and true
On the [C]twen-ty-fifth of Elul
The [G]wall stands firm and new
Our enemies hear the news
Their [Em]confidence sinks low
They [C]know this work was accomplished
[G]By our God a[D]lone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
A[G]zariah son of Maaseiah
Be[Em]side his house he stands
Next to [C]Benjamin and Hasshub
Re[G]building by God's com[D]mand
Son [G]of Ananiah he is
In the [Em]list of the brave
Working [C]on the wall of the city
Where the [G]faithful have [D]grave
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
The [G]nations around were afraid
When the [Em]wall rose high
For they [C]knew the hand of the Lord
Was the [G]one who did [D]this
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
So we [Em]set our hands to the good work
And the [C]wall [D]rises [G]high
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
